Z||000007||Oreif||02-22-2000||01:24 AM||||My goal is to redo the entire suspension and brakes! I've already started on the front suspension. It's nice to have a relative who can get parts powder-coated for free! Front is waiting for warmer weather to put it back together. Hoping to have it all completed by May.||||reg||6
Z||000008||batboy||02-22-2000||01:44 AM||||Hey Cooter, if you're really serious about selling the ol' 'burb, let me know. Mine's just about on it's last legs, but I said that a year ago too. It's got 266,000 miles on the clock and pieces of rusty quarter panels falling off in large hunks. Fluids are leaking out of about every seal too. I'll trade you a Fiero for it...your wife will LOVE that...LOL!||||reg||1
Z||000009||wkayl||02-22-2000||01:48 AM||||Wash, wax and drive.  I have plans to go to Sisseton S Dak the first weekend in June for a car show.||||reg||1
Z||000010||2M4 Dale||02-22-2000||06:31 AM||||Over the winter I've gotten most of the mechanicals done and installed a new sound system. As far as Spring goes, I hope to get my coupe into a body shop within the next month.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DJRice||02-22-2000||09:47 AM||||I am going to replace the nose on my car.  It is sagging a bit, I think the previous owner bumped something.  Its been bothering me for almost 2 years now, and I have a new nose to put on it, but havent had the chance.<P>Then it will need paint. <P>Im thinking nows a good time to replace the dew wipes as well, because my drivers door handle needs some TLC anyway.  I just ordered Rodney Dickman's Dew Wipe tool to see if I can make that job go easier.<P>Thats the easy stuff... I am really itching to add a vista vent.  Its kinda funny, I will drop an engine in a heartbeat, but I am kinda leary about taking off my roof.<P>So many projects, so little time, even less cash flow...||||reg||1
Z||000012||87ECO5||02-22-2000||09:58 AM||||Needs:  New starter, exhaust manifold, tires.<P>Wants:  Engine detailing, new carpet, new seats or seat covers, resurface the "hi-tech" aluminum rims, CD player.||||reg||1
Z||000013||turbo86se||02-22-2000||10:36 AM||||bhooper & Carolina GT, you're not too far away from me, LMK if you want to get together sometime! I'm in Myrtle Beach.<BR> <BR>My spring projects include selling my black decklid with factory spoiler and 5" wingstands, buying TOM's scoop, and installing that with a factory spoiler on my 86SE. I also need some custom rims on the SE.<BR>  <BR>batboy, that front-mounted battery sounds interesting. Where did you get the bracket? Sounds like a good idea, please tell me about it!<BR> <BR>Spring projects for my 88 coupe: New carpet, door hinges, clean up the rusting straight pipe where my cat used to be. You should see my driveway! Maybe new seat covers!<p>[This message has been edited by turbo86se (edited 02-22-2000).]||||reg||6
