Z||000017||mshill||02-22-2000||04:00 PM||||batboy,  thanks to a 3 car garage, I do my projects in the winter so I can drive the car during the spring and summer.  It (86SE V6) has been out of comission since mid-January for a 2.8L rebuild (with +1 cam), new clutch, fixing exhaust leak, poly rear suspension, bushings, poly cradle bushings, fresh motor mounts, belts and hoses.<P>I am planning on putting flywheel and clutch on and dropping the engine back into the cradle this week. Need to clean up the wiring harnesses, put accessories back on and move my springs over to the new struts before I stuff it all back into the car.<P>When all done, it should be just about all brand new.  Sure hope it drives that way.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000018||Monkeyman||02-22-2000||05:14 PM||||I plan to actually get my '85 GT, either rebuild the motor or find a good used one, put new seats in it from a '93 Z24 Cav (thanx anonymous forum member), begin to install a killer stereo system, add the Rally gauges, and get a backlit GT instrument cluster.||||reg||1
Z||000019||fiero56||02-22-2000||05:39 PM||||I'm looking at the possibility of overhauling/rebuilding a "new" 2.8 for my Formula. I'm thinking a 3.1 or 3.2. Plus, it would be nice to replace shift and select cables, engine and tranny mounts, stereo, front rack bushings, poly bushings on the rear sway bar, a short shifter kit from Rodney Dickman, and completely strip and repaint my wheels(there are a few spots were the clearcoat is flaking. Plus a new Borla exhaust system would be nice. I'm sure new projects will surface as well.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 02-22-2000).]||||reg||1
