Z||000022||batboy||02-22-2000||09:52 PM||||Spyder and Turbo, I got my battery kit that mounts under the spare tire from Chris West of West Coast Fiero. It's a little expensive, but is strong (heavy gauge aluminum), the design is well thought out, and it's good quality construction. However... I was a little unhappy at they way I was treated. First he claimed I never sent him a check, my Credit Union had the cancelled and cleared check to prove I did. Then I waited and waited and waited. Eventually, he quit answering my emails. Months later, I finally did receive it though. I've never heard anyone say that Chris ripped them off and I don't believe he would intentionally do this, but I have heard from others that long waits for his shipments are common. That box on the V8 Archie site looks similar, but I don't know anything about it. Relocating the battery up front is almost mandatory with a V8 conversion. Here is a pic of the style I got.<P> <IMG SRC="http://207.182.229.65/Upgrades/Upgr_gif/Batbox.gif"> ||||reg||1
